# TERMINATION. A subseteq B, B subseteq A is an ordinary equivalence, not an error.
# Without subtracting conclusions from the ACCUMULATED store, CR1 re-derives both
# every round, a batch-only dedup keeps them, the frontier never empties, and this
# perfectly coherent ontology burns its budget and returns inconclusive forever.
# Expect: FIXPOINT, coherent, and A/B mutually subsuming.

@prefix :    <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf :B .
:B rdfs:subClassOf :A .
